<!--
  Letter B, drawn as one outline with evenOdd so the two counters are holes.

  The previous version put two solid rounded blocks side by side, which at
  toolbar size read as one dark smudge: there were no counters at all. The
  attempt after that restored the counters but left the upper one at about
  70% of the lower one's area while the stem stayed 2.9 units of a 9.6 unit
  tall glyph. A stem that heavy next to two cramped holes reads as lumpy
  rather than as a letter.

  Proportions now: a 2.0 unit stem on a 14.4 unit tall glyph, the upper
  counter 4.0 x 4.2 and the lower 4.3 x 5.0, so the upper is about 78% of
  the lower by area. That is the usual relationship for a B, where the lower
  bowl is the larger one, but close enough that the pair looks deliberate.

  The glyph is centred on x=12 and spans y 3.4 to 17.8, leaving a little more
  room below than above, which is where the eye expects the weight.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp" android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24" android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path android:fillColor="@color/fg_default"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M8,3.4h5.6c2.5,0 4.2,1.4 4.2,3.5c0,1.4 -0.7,2.4 -1.9,2.9c1.6,0.5 2.5,1.7 2.5,3.4c0,2.4 -1.9,4.1 -4.6,4.1H8zM10,5.6v4.2h3.1c1.4,0 2.3,-0.8 2.3,-2.1c0,-1.3 -0.9,-2.1 -2.3,-2.1zM10,11.6v5.7h3.5c1.7,0 2.7,-1.1 2.7,-2.8c0,-1.8 -1,-2.9 -2.7,-2.9z" />
